      "id": 1,
      "text": "Granite Falls was founded in 1883 after gold and silver were found in nearby Monte Cristo mines, spurring rapid growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granite_Falls%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from the granite‑covered falls on the South Fork Stillaguamish, just a couple miles north of town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.historylink.org/File/8532"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1892 the Everett and Monte Cristo Railway reached Granite Falls, building a station that linked the town to the booming mining region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
